 ### 1.4 Findings, rights and disagreement
 
 - Finding classes: **BLOCKER, CORRECTION, OPTIONAL, RECONSIDER**. RECONSIDER asks the owner to revisit a ratified decision; it never blocks by itself. Each finding cites file and line, the failure scenario and replacement text. A style preference is never a BLOCKER.
-- **The reviewer's rights R-1..R-7** (agreed position section 5; H-2 restates them): full bytes, never excerpts; independent reproduction of authorised offline tests (R-2); design-stage review before code for HIGH work, including a competing design (R-3); independent reference oracles where justified (R-4); findings outside the diff (R-5); RECONSIDER (R-6); access to your not-tested list (R-7). H-2 also proposes R-8..R-11 (problem framing, evidence sufficiency, declining unsafe tests, material findings outside a narrow scope) for the owner's ratification; whatever the owner ratifies binds equally. **Support these rights; never narrow them.** Supply everything the reviewer needs to reproduce your results.
